      },
      "source": [
        "# ML-10 — Content Action Playbook\n",
        "\n",
        "This skeleton is yours to fill. Work the sections **in order** — each one has a one-line hint. Simple words, honest numbers.\n",
        "\n",
        "> Working with an AI assistant? Tell it to read `skills/README.md` first and load the one skill this assignment names on its card."
      ],
      "id": "JyekqRE_P2Oq"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "zBvYFfFPP2Or"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 1. Ranked actions + reason codes\n",
        "\n",
        "*The queue: what to do first, and why, in words a human trusts.*"
      ],
      "id": "zBvYFfFPP2Or"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Action 1: Refresh & Expand Content (Top Priority)\n",
        "\n",
        "Reason Code: HIGH_IMPRESSIONS_LOW_CTR\n",
        "\n",
        "Trigger: Predicted clicks > 1000, but actual past CTR < 3%.\n",
        "\n",
        "Why trust this: The model confirms high visibility (impressions). The low CTR suggests the title/meta description needs immediate optimization to capture existing demand.\n",
        "\n",
        "Action 2: Investigate Ranking Drop (Secondary Priority)\n",
        "\n",
        "Reason Code: SUDDEN_POSITION_DROP\n",
        "\n",
        "Trigger: Average position dropped by > 3 spots week-over-week.\n",
        "\n",
        "Why trust this: Organic traffic is highly sensitive to position changes on page 1. This action flags URLs that require a technical or content audit."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "zbXkHkpFP2Os"
      },
      "id": "zbXkHkpFP2Os"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0LUsO-ftP2Os"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 2. Intended use and limits\n",
        "\n",
        "*Who uses this, for what — and where it stops being valid.*"
      ],
      "id": "0LUsO-ftP2Os"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Intended Use:\n",
        "This playbook is designed for content and SEO teams to prioritize their weekly optimization queues. It highlights pages with the highest potential return on investment and flags urgent ranking issues.\n",
        "\n",
        "Limits (Where it stops being valid):\n",
        "\n",
        "Seasonality: The model does not account for sudden seasonal spikes. Recommendations during anomalous traffic periods should be paused.\n",
        "\n",
        "Brand vs. Non-Brand: The model treats all queries equally and cannot distinguish if a high CTR is simply due to a branded search term.\n",
        "\n",
        "New Content: This playbook relies on historical data. It cannot provide reliable actions for brand-new URLs with less than 30 days of history."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "FcXwCmi7P2Os"
      },
      "id": "FcXwCmi7P2Os"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "zc_saHznP2Os"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 3. Human review + the no-go list\n",
        "\n",
        "*What a person must check before acting. What should never be automated.*"
      ],
      "id": "zc_saHznP2Os"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Human Review Required Before Acting:\n",
        "\n",
        "Title/Meta Changes: Before changing a title tag for HIGH_IMPRESSIONS_LOW_CTR, a human must review the actual SERP to ensure the new title matches user intent.\n",
        "\n",
        "Technical Audits: For SUDDEN_POSITION_DROP, a human must check Google Search Console for manual actions or crawl errors before rewriting content.\n",
        "\n",
        "The No-Go List (Never Automate):\n",
        "\n",
        "Automated Deletions: Never automatically delete or redirect a page based solely on low predicted clicks.\n",
        "\n",
        "Automated Keyword Stuffing: Never allow a script to automatically inject keywords into titles based on model outputs without editorial review."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "RqjbXgCiP2Os"
      },
      "id": "RqjbXgCiP2Os"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "JyQ-fzx_P2Ot"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 4. Monitoring / retrain triggers\n",
        "\n",
        "*What would tell you the recommendations went stale?*"
      ],
      "id": "JyQ-fzx_P2Ot"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Monitoring Triggers (When recommendations went stale):\n",
        "\n",
        "Data Drift: Monitor the distribution of daily impressions. If the overall volume drops by more than 20% compared to the training data baseline, the predictions are likely stale.\n",
        "\n",
        "Algorithm Updates: If Google announces a confirmed core update, pause playbook actions for 14 days until SERP volatility settles.\n",
        "\n",
        "Retrain Triggers:\n",
        "\n",
        "Time-based: The model must be retrained every 30 days with fresh GSC data to capture shifting search trends.\n",
        "\n",
        "Performance-based: If the R2 score of the baseline model drops below 0.35 on a rolling 7-day validation set, trigger an immediate retrain."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "YaF_P4tVP2Ot"
      },
      "id": "YaF_P4tVP2Ot"
    },
    {
